Here’s a basic **privacy-focused browser extension** that blocks tracking scripts using **JavaScript/TypeScript** (the most recommended choice for browser extensions). This example uses the **WebExtensions API**, which works in **Chrome, Firefox, Edge, and other modern browsers**.

---

### **1. File Structure**
```
privacy-blocker/
├── manifest.json       (Extension metadata)
├── background.js       (Background script for blocking)
├── content.js          (Content script for DOM manipulation)
└── popup/
    ├── popup.html      (UI for user settings)
    └── popup.js        (Handles user interactions)
```

---

### **2. `manifest.json` (Required for Browser Extensions)**
```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Privacy Blocker",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Blocks tracking scripts for better privacy.",
  "permissions": [
    "webRequest",
    "webRequestBlocking",
    "storage",
    "activeTab"
  ],
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"]
    }
  ],
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup/popup.html",
    "default_icon": {
      "16": "icons/icon16.png",
      "48": "icons/icon48.png",
      "128": "icons/icon128.png"
    }
  },
  "icons": {
    "16": "icons/icon16.png",
    "48": "icons/icon48.png",
    "128": "icons/icon128.png"
  }
}
```
- **`webRequest`** and **`webRequestBlocking`** allow blocking network requests.
- **`content_scripts`** injects `content.js` into every page.
- **`action`** defines the extension’s popup UI.

---

### **3. `background.js` (Blocks Tracking Scripts)**
```javascript
// List of known tracking domains (can be expanded)
const TRACKING_DOMAINS = [
  "google-analytics.com",
  "doubleclick.net",
  "facebook.com/tr",
  "adservice.google.com",
  "googletagmanager.com",
  "analytics.yahoo.com",
  "scorecardresearch.com"
];

// Block tracking scripts
chrome.webRequest.onBeforeRequest.addListener(
  (details) => {
    const url = new URL(details.url);
    if (TRACKING_DOMAINS.some(domain => url.hostname.includes(domain))) {
      console.log(`Blocked tracking script: ${url.hostname}`);
      return { cancel: true }; // Block the request
    }
    return { cancel: false }; // Allow the request
  },
  { urls: ["<all_urls>"] },
  ["blocking"]
);
```
- Uses **`chrome.webRequest`** to intercept and block tracking scripts.
- **`TRACKING_DOMAINS`** can be expanded with more trackers.

---

